## ANIMATION CONTROLLERS (2)

### `animationController` (`alwaysDirty`)
- Inputs: `signal_0..signal_7: SIGNAL`, `config: CONFIG` (optional, supplies labels + default min/max). Outputs: `animation: ANIMATION` keyed `'0'..'7'`. Params: `min_i / max_i` per slot (defaults 0/1).
- Resolves active effect via `inputs.config.__effectName` and pulls `effect.animation.slots` for default min/max + labels. Per slot: `min/max` priority `param → slot default → 0/1`; reads `inputs.signal_i`; builds `ChannelSignal { time: signal.value, raw: clamp01, value: lerp, state }`.
- Output handle named `animation` (not `signal`) so it doesn't collide with SIGNAL outputs of Timer/Interpolator/Combine/SignalSwitch. Every channel always emitted (`value = lerp(min, max, 0)` when unwired).

### `animationSwitch` (`alwaysDirty`)
- Inputs: `animation_a` (`a`), `animation_b` (`b`), `event: EVENT`. Outputs: `animation: ANIMATION`. Params: same as `signalSwitch`.
- Same event-toggle + cross-fade contract as `signalSwitch`, applied to whole `AnimationSignal` packets at once. Cross-fade is per channel and per scalar field (`time/raw/value` lerp, `state` is OR). Channels missing on one side lerp against an idle channel (active channels never drop).
- Use to swap whole control surfaces (calm preset ↔ intense preset on a single Emit) instead of fanning 8 SignalSwitches. Reuses `applyEasing` / `SwitchProfile` / `SwitchSide` from `signal-switch.ts`.

