## OUTPUT (4)

### `effect` (`alwaysDirty`)
- Inputs: `source: TEXTURE`, `txcn0..txcn7: TEXTURE`, `contour: CONTOUR`, `animation: ANIMATION`, `config: CONFIG`. Outputs: `texture: TEXTURE`, `metrics: METRICS`. Params: `{}` (uniforms come from upstream Config + animation slots).
- See `effects-and-shaders.mdc → Runtime: EffectProcessor`. Compiles passes on demand, builds `UniformGroup` from fields + animation pool + texture pool, renders all passes into a single output RT in one `renderer.render`, emits per-pass CPU + total GPU dispatch metrics.
- State: `cachedEffectName`, `warnedConfigs`. Per-pass meshes/geometries NOT cached — rebuilt every frame. View re-labels `txcn{i}` from upstream Config's `textures.slots`. Per-frame uniform overrides from `inputs.config[uName]`; missing keys fall back to `FieldDef.default`.

### `preview`
- Not `alwaysDirty`. Inputs: `texture`. Outputs: `texture` (pass-through), `_canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`.
- Pass-through propagates downstream every tick. Throttled extract (33 ms): `renderer.extract.pixels` → Canvas2D; force `A = 255` so transparent regions show as opaque previews.
- State: single reused `Texture` wrapper (`extractTex` / `extractTexSrc`) — recreated only when upstream source identity changes. `imgCanvas`, `extracting`, `lastExtractTime`. **Single-wrapper rule was the dominant memory leak fix** — never allocate a fresh `Texture({ source })` per frame. `destroy()` releases the wrapper but never the upstream source.

### `contourPreview`
- Not `alwaysDirty`. Inputs: `contour: CONTOUR`. No outputs. Stores latest contour on `proc.contour`. View reads it directly (`engine.getProcessor(id).contour`) → outline + sample dots on Canvas2D. Cheap to leave wired.

### `publishRoot`
- `output`. Not `alwaysDirty`. Inputs: `texture: TEXTURE`. Outputs: `texture: TEXTURE` (pass-through — chain into Preview to confirm "what the supplier sees"). Params: `name: 'Untitled'`, `version: 'v1'`, `effectId: ''` (auto-slugified, lowercase ASCII alphanumerics + hyphen, capped 64).
- Pure pass-through. Marked traversal entry point; rides upstream Effect's dirty propagation.
- Exactly one per scene supported. `derivePublishedSurface` reports both `no-root` and `multiple-roots` as hard errors. `effectId` required (`effect-id-missing` if blank). View shows live publication summary; same panel in `PublishInspector`.

